LingTu changes (2026-10-30/31) include the C++ implementation over immutable
OctoMap columns, per-height closing, separate inferred support storage,
occupied-height acceleration blocks and native XYZ A* integration.
surface_graph.cpp and route_smoothing.cpp adapt the pinned revision's
multi-source Voronoi corridors, string pulling and elastic-path update ideas
from nodes.rs, edges.rs, planner.rs and smoother.rs.

2026-11-08. SurfaceIndex moved to src/maps/cpp/layers/surface.cpp for reuse by
navigation and mapd. Its attribution remains in src/maps/SURFACE_NOTICE.

2026-11-15/16. src/kernels/nav/mls_core supplies Rust surface preparation and
sparse graph queries through the C ABI. OctoMap supplies raw occupancy.
C++ performs the final robot support, body, step, slope and swept-path checks.
The standalone C++ SurfaceGraph remains available for regression tests.
The historical SurfaceIndex comparison tool has been retired.

